Z||000009||COUNTIBLIS||02-05-2001||01:10 AM||||I love it!  Yeah they play for a million at the big game and the team splits it.  I think that it will get better.  More cities will get teams and the watch out NFL!  To me there was more electricity out there on the field.  Kinda reminds me when I played back in college and high school.  In order for these guys to make money they have to win.  That will make anyone play or work harder.  <P><BR>Later <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tigger||02-05-2001||08:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>Cheerleaders and silicone right on.  Most of them were blonds too. duh  Lets have some more of the upward shots from the cheerleaders knee level. duh!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, I found that was the best part of the game! j/k<P>I think it was ok.  The camera angles were cool.  Kinda neat to watch a play with a camera guy on the field.<P>They switched views too quickly tho, need to keep focus on one camera for more than 10s at a time.  I thought I was watching NYPD Blue.<P>Do they have a team from MI in the league?<P>||||reg||14
